<title>LUXEMBOURG: Safra Q2 profit rises 35  pct.</title>
<headline>Safra Q2 profit rises 35  pct.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months ended June 30.</p>
<p>				   (million dollars unless stated)</p>
<p> Group net			62.4		vs 46.2</p>
<p> Group net per share	  1.77		vs 1.31</p>
<p> Interest income		270.9	     vs 249.8</p>
<p> Interest expense	     195.3	     vs 181.2</p>
<p>Six Months</p>
<p> Group net			119.6	     vs 90.3</p>
<p> Group net per share	  3.39		vs 2.56</p>
<p> Interest income		138.2	     vs 126.0</p>
<p> Interest expense	     369.3	     vs 362.0</p>
<p>Note - Full name of private banking group is Safra Republic Holdings SA -- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
